        "id": 1561651
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-20T05:50:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From the doc on DownloadManager: \"Apps that request downloads through this API should register a broadcast receiver for ACTION_NOTIFICATION_CLICKED to appropriately handle when the user clicks on a running download in a notification or from the downloads UI.\"\n\nWill the download show up as a notification? Can the user dismiss it?",
      "revId": "6333603fbd44dab2e1ef6070d8257a8802f6aa25",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4c4350a5_7faaeb32",
        "filename": "networksecurity/service/src/com/android/server/net/ct/DownloadHelper.java",
        "patchSetId": 24
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1929300
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-20T12:03:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For system_server it looks like the default setting is overridden to not show a notification, or maybe the download is just too quick and the notification does not have time to appear.\n\nConsidering we are going to trigger a download every day and most users won\u0027t know what data is being downloaded, I would be more in favor of not having a download notification. I added a line setting `VISIBILITY_HIDDEN` at request construction.",
      "parentUuid": "7227f2ab_83dbaa3e",
      "revId": "6333603fbd44dab2e1ef6070d8257a8802f6aa25",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
